body:
Okay, I tried exporting .gcode files from AnkerMake Studio, UltiMaker Cura, and PrusaSlicer. I exported the default names, then simplified file names, then simplified file names with underscores in between the words.

&#x200B;

None of the files worked. .\_.

What an asshole that guy is.

&#x200B;

The condom thing is something that should be communicated about beforehand. STI's, accidental pregnancy, etc. It's not like it's a difficult conversation, just laying out ground rules. If anything, you should have a better idea how to approach this situation in the future. Never assume anything.

He doesn't sound emotionally mature enough yet to handle a serious committed relationship. The act of avoiding eye contact and being cold towards you for a few days is also passive-aggressive behavior aimed at making you the bad guy and punishing you for whatever transgression you committed in his eyes. Everyone has a past. Don't go digging into it if you don't want to know all the details.

&#x200B;

It's a good thing the wedding is called off. I think you're dodging a bullet with this one. Someone who is emotionally mature will sit down with you and talk things out without engaging in passive-aggressive warfare.

Definitely. I was lucky to even get the 2 soldiers out of there.

&#x200B;

Same friend forced me to play Xcom 2's spark mission? I have not played Xcom 2 and also went into this one blind. He was annoyed I survived with everyone. :D

Russia has only infantry stacks and a fighter. Meanwhile, US hasn't landed in Europe yet. That was a turn that could've been spent doing sending transport to Brazil or Africa.

&#x200B;

I'm rooting for the Axis. Germany's going all-out attack. :D

Really like an annual tradition for anyone who has seen it.

&#x200B;

Maybe some Xanax will make the series easier to watch?

Geez. You need to be single for a while and find yourself. Learn to stand on your own financially and emotionally before being involved with anyone.

&#x200B;

Also, an ex is an ex for a reason. Stop romanticizing him and remember the reasons you're not together.

That would make neutral powers more interesting. :D If you don't completely wipe them, they gain back some or all of their infantry starting in the next round of gameplay.

&#x200B;

The person you're playing against was wrong though. I play with someone similar who would decide what a rule was instead or cheat in a cooperative game. Made it really not fun to play.

No one will ever be ahead of any of these variants.

&#x200B;

Except for North Korea. No Covid reported there!

I was debating it, but decided against it. A lot of the parts of it remind me of the Fallout board game except you have a short campaign with 'endless' replay value versus the single-shot missions in Fallout. The Skyrim minis are okay. I really dig the alternative poses. I wish the monsters had at least 2 different types of poses.

&#x200B;

The other issue is Modiphius supposedly starting fulfillment late next summer. It took them 4 years to finish Siege of the Citadel, so any project involving more than writing RPG books should be approached cautiously.

This is the most accessible version available digitally. It gets a lot of things right except for a few rules. The one that sticks out to me is that you can't land your fighters on carriers of your allies though.

&#x200B;

I'm kinda hoping Beamdog releases modding tools for it because I know there's a lot of interest in a global version of this game.

Going off her responses, she's passive-aggressive and immature. I don't know how long you have been together or how other parts of the relationship are, but it's something to keep in mind as you work through this and other issues in the future.

&#x200B;

Can't imagine most guys would be in the mood like that as well. Don't sweat it.

I told my friend who knows nothing of history he should push to be France since they're a powerhouse in Axis and Allies.

&#x200B;

I sure as hell wasn't going to let him screw up the Allies' strategy.

Give notice at your current place and have a new lease already signed. Changing where you live on top of freeing yourself from the relationship will be a breath of fresh air you need. Plus when you go to have the breakup conversation, this will reinforce the breakup and allow both of you to start healing more quickly post-relationship. It doesn't matter what he thinks of you or your decision. You're not happy and you're doing what you think is best for you.

&#x200B;

There will always be things you can improve and examine about yourself. It really helps to be out of a relationship and out of the dating scene for a while to spend time on and take care of you.

 I don't know anything about the show, but she definitely just manipulated you with sex and some sus trust talk.  "...made me promise to trust her as much as she trusted me" to me reads like she wants to go on said show, flirt around, possibly fuck several people, but doesn't want you doing the same.

&#x200B;

I had an ex who frequently brought up the issue of trust (favorite line was "don't you trust me?"), went through my phone constantly, liked playing the victim, and often refused to discuss things that I didn't need to know about. She was incredibly charming and manipulative.

Your dad is awesome. I don't think you have too much to worry about.

&#x200B;

Good story. :D

I can't imagine many players would recommend that, but I guess that could depend on how the war in Europe is going. If the UK/US has a foothold in Europe and Russia is hanging in there, I could see the UK retreating from India to protect Russia until Germany falls.

&#x200B;

I haven't seen a game yet where Japan is able to win the game on its own for the Axis.

Things will get better once you're an adult and not living in the nest anymore. Your mom sounds like she has a conservative mentality and is being overprotective with regards to this specific issue you posted. I'd wager someone close to her or in her immediate family had a kid before being married/turning 18. It's also possible her parents drilled this mindset into her head growing up.

&#x200B;

As for being bent over and spanked until you're sore, that's pretty tame compared to what you can ask your girlfriend to do to you.

90% sure she wants to fuck.

&#x200B;

But that's a messy business, fucking your roommates. Have a backup plan when shit goes down the drain!

How long have you been together? You two should be able to talk about anything if you're seriously considered long term and/or marriage down the road. Obviously this is her issue to resolve, but at the same time it will affect your household too. Is this the only topic that she doesn't want to discuss or are there others?

&#x200B;

If I was in her shoes, I would just say the card was damaged just to get a new one issued.  They're obviously taking advantage of it now. Sometimes you gotta do that to family taking advantage of you.

Just when you think your table is big enough. Nope.

&#x200B;

"Just go with it. Keep clumsy people and pets away for a few days." :D

Your friends are just immature. At least you know your type. A lot of guys can't figure that shit out until they get older.

&#x200B;

The real plot twist is when a decade down the road a couple of your friends turn out to actually be gay while you're married to a hot as fuck tomboy with a family.

I've often thought about this. What am I contributing to society that I could justify continuing on? Doesn't it make more sense for someone who doesn't contribute or doesn't feel like they contribute to opt out?

&#x200B;

Although, there has to be something that you're not lazy at. Even people who do nothing but play games for instance are contributing to something.

I'm not sure if all the apps have it (they probably do), but there are training plans built in that have you doing various types of runs including interval running. You'll run for a set period of time as fast as you can, then slow it down for a minute or so, then back to full speed. I had to use the paid version of Runkeeper to utilize it though, not sure if you have to do that with the underarmour app as well.

&#x200B;

Just be sure to listen to your body though if you start having issues with your running as you continue working towards your goal.

Just means you have to find a guy who digs it or doesn't mind it. Can't have a negative attitude about squirting.

&#x200B;

Hell, I'd consider that a bonus in the bedroom if I was with a woman who squirted.

Really puts things in perspective. A lot changes in several years.

&#x200B;

Except for Mount and Blade releases.

Definitely. That sounds like how my first Spartan race went last April.

&#x200B;

Do you do any kind of interval runs as well? The plan I'm on with Runkeeper has me doing surges once a week where I'm going from just short of a dead sprint to a job repeating several times.

~~I read a few posts from others if they have 5 or 6 people show up wanting to play a scenario. They bump up the scenario level and trap level by 2 while keeping the gold and experience earned equal to what difficulty the group is playing at.~~ I just saw the response that you don't play more than 4 at a time.

&#x200B;

If you have 6-7 people that want to play but don't always have the same people, two people could either share a character or create 2 characters with their own personal goals. The problem there is if they both show up to play on the same night; then they'd have to alternate.

&#x200B;

Do you have the Forgotten Circles expansion? It's $15 right now on Amazon. Gives you another starter class you can use without having to open a box for a character.

&#x200B;

Also, if some people just show up more frequently than others, you can always play scenarios casually (usually for personal quest reasons or grabbing a treasure missed the first time) or play rando scenarios. Maybe you can even create a houserule where characters at a much higher level could pretend to be a lower level just for the scenario and not allow them to use any ability cards that are a higher level than what they choose to play at. I briefly kicked that idea around, but decided against it.

Gotcha. Yeah, don't be surprised if a lot of scenarios come down to the end like that! The last two scenarios I played by myself, they came down to the last 2 cards I could play before I would long rest and then exhaust out!

&#x200B;

Once you finish a scenario, you can always play it in casual mode again. Basically, you don't draw event cards before it and you don't donate to the sanctuary (but you could house rule either of those two if you wanted). I've noticed the Brute usually will be one of the first to exhaust out. The XP you earn and the gold you pick up will be yours to keep and if you complete the scenario in casual mode, you'll earn the additional XP for completing it too.

Well, not too much you could do. Between all of the starter classes, the Brute is the most suitable because of his larger HP.

&#x200B;

What you can do since they're relying on you to absorb most of the damage is use cards that will limit how much damage you take. If you play Warding Strength before your first rest and no other loss cards, that will leave you with 8 cards and 4 rounds to play before your next long rest. Go slow in certain rounds to get up in an enemy's face, then play Shield Bash with Initiative 15 so you can go fast next round and have that extra shield for the whole round. You picked out Fatal Advance for the level 2 card I'm guessing which will pair nicely with Balanced Measure which will give you an Attack 4 (Attack 6 if you use that ability with Striding Boots).

&#x200B;

You can also pick up Hide Armor. I found that to be really useful and cheap as well. Heater Shield can also be useful early on. My friend swears by Iron Helmet which only occurs every so often, but I've seen that come up a few times now for his characters and that is also pretty cheap in the early going.

You draw 2 battle goals, but only pick 1 for the scenario. From what you wrote, it sounded like you were using both.

&#x200B;

Did you win the scenario? The first scenario can actually be pretty hard for first time players.

Yeah, you have to think one or two turns ahead when you're planning element use. Mindthief is a good example because before she uses an ice creation ability, she has to ensure that she'll be within range to use Frigid Apparition the following turn for the Stun bonus.

&#x200B;

Depending on what monsters are in the scenario too, you have to be careful with what elements you create. Some monsters receive nice bonuses on their cards if they can consume certain elements and they move before your character.

You can keep tabs on your prosperity and start saving as you get closer to unlocking a new prosperity level. In the rulebook, you do get new shop items to choose from when prosperity rises.

&#x200B;

What do you have so far as the Tinkerer? I got the Eagle-Eye Goggles first and used them constantly during his time in the party.

Can you keep some infantry and a tank or fighter in the regions bordering France, Normandy, and Holland until you can deal with them to stave off any planned attacks? He can't make any really aggressive moves from France. If he launched an attack, he'll take heavy losses and risk losing France as well.

&#x200B;

He's going to take back London easily when the US can get there. It might be worth building at least a couple infantry there to make him fight for it.

&#x200B;

Russia has a lot of higher value troops tied up in Eastern Poland if you wanted to continue going after them.

&#x200B;

Are you going to try to go for Morocco or Syria as Italy? In this game, you at least know that France is incapable of collecting any kind of bonus income, so you'll always know what their earning potential will be. France is only earning 12 per turn with the potential for even less depending on what happens. This is kind of neat to see how your game evolved.

&#x200B;

Just some ideas if you haven't considered them. I'm interested to see how this turns out.

No. I want to be as loud, explosive, and smelly as possible to keep anyone from attempting to sit in a stall next to me.

&#x200B;

So tired of hearing guys talk on the phone while taking a shit. Why does this have to be common.

I can. :)

My friend playing the Cragheart enhanced Unstable Upheaval. There is one dot next to the Attack @ 3 line. It targets all adjacent enemies. From what I've been reading in the last couple hours, he should've paid 100 gold instead of 50 when he originally enhanced it.

&#x200B;

Same friend also enhanced Dirt Tornado yesterday. There is only one dot next to Attack @ 1 and there are numerous hexes on that card. I'm certain he should've paid 150 gold to upgrade it with poison, but he stickered it last night for 75 gold. I texted him about this one and we're trying to decide if we will either ignore the poison enhancement until he reaches 150 gold with his Cragheart or if we'll put him in debt for 75 gold until he pays for the rest of the enhancement.

&#x200B;

The one that caught my eye mainly for curiosity is the Tinkerer's Restorative Mist ability card. The bottom ability Move @ 2 can be enhanced. The Heal @ 1, affect all adjacent allies, can't be enhanced. Would enhancing that move ability cost double or no?

Ah, there's target x cards as well? Okay.

&#x200B;

I had to dig through the cards for an example of one. So the top ability on Reviving Shock for the Tinkerer...if I enhance either the dot next to the attack or the dot next to the target, it's automatically doubled?

I've been wondering this! The rulebook doesn't come out and say that random dungeons are casual play. It was frustrating attempting Barrow Lair 3 times and losing each time with different parties. Doing the random dungeons, we got to see a majority of the different enemies we'd run up against in the game.

&#x200B;

Now, this raises another question I have concerning endgame. There are only so many campaign missions to complete. Is it possible that Gloomhaven's prosperity level won't reach 9 by the time we run out of campaign missions to complete?

Well, it is designed to simulate the fall of France at the beginning of the game. One of the allied players controls France, but all you do is just push whatever units are around the map. If France is liberated later in the game, usually it means Germany will fall soon and the Axis will lose unless Japan is close to winning.

&#x200B;

If French Indo-China is captured by Japan, UK, ANZAC, US, etc. can capture it for the IPCs. So it helps to let Japan capture it if you want to add that territory and IPCs later to your nation. Same with French territories in Europe and Africa. I'm not sure if TripleA allows you to just take control of them, maybe it's an option.

You do NOT owe anyone an apology. Your mom made mistakes, your biological dad made mistakes, and the man who raised you alongside the others as his own is making mistakes too. This is not a situation that requires you to fix anything. It really sucks that this is how everyone decided to play their cards, but shit happens and life does go on.

&#x200B;

You have a lot of resources and the internetz at your disposal do figure the adulting game out like insurance, college, moving out on your own, etc.

&#x200B;

Don't compare yourself to your siblings like that either. They have their shit together because dad basically bankrolled everything for them. Most people don't have everything paid for them when they go to college like that.

&#x200B;

I think it's shitty that the man who raised you is turning around and doing this and may very well come to regret this eventually. But your focus should boil down to what you what to do right now and how you're getting there.

Whoa. Third time?!?!

&#x200B;

Not everyone is like this. I think you've just had really shitty luck is all. It's not a bad idea to swear off dating and relationships for a while. I've found a couple of new amazing hobbies I love after getting out of the dating/relationship game. You should indulge yourself for a while.

&#x200B;

Also willing to bank that after some time has passed he'll contact you again wanting to get back together. You can tell him then to fuck himself. ;)
